                <pb facs="0692" n="594" sameAs="frus:frus1900/pg594"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Choate to Mr.
                            Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1900-02-22"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">February 22,
                    1900</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Choate reports that the foreign office had not, until his inquiry, learned
                    of the seizure of the <hi rendition="#italic">Sabine</hi>, but that inquiries
                    will at once be instituted and the results reported to him. He requests to be
                    advised of date and place of seizure and present whereabouts of the vessel.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
